celona final, Barrowman again broke his world record, finishing in 2:10.16 to win gold, as he was in control from start-to-finish and won comfortably. He was followed by Hungarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/48228"} "Norbert Rózsa"] ", also second in the 100 breast in Barcelona, and Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/47268"} "Nick Gillingham"] ", as the podium was exactly as it had been at the 1991 Worlds. Gillingham had won silver in the event in 1988, and had also broken a world record in the 200 since Seoul, but that had then been bettered by Barrowman five times."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "601"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51260"} "Mike Barrowman"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "2:11.48 (1 h7)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2:10.16 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "335"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/48228"} "Norbert Rózsa"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "2:12.95 (2 h7)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2:11.23 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "246"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47268"} "Nick Gillingham"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "2:13.42 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2:11.29 